      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We present the case of a 66 year old patient with a heterogeneous clinical course over ten months, particularly worsening of vision, hearing and hip pain. She finally died of multi-organ failure. The increased wear of a metal-on-metal hip implant lead to cobalt intoxication. The crucial therapy consists in removing the cobalt source. In the future, physicians need to be aware of this insidious and life-threatening disease possibly affecting thousands of patients after total hip replacement."},
